{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa in Cooking School: Italian Food"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Italian Food Traditions"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Delicious Food > Italy"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Count and Non-Count Nouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Count nouns are things we can count.<br /><br /><ul><li>They can be singular or plural (a casserole, two casseroles).  </li> <li>You can use <span class=\"strong\">some </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">any </span>  with count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">       \tExample: some recipes</span>  <li>You can also use <span class=\"strong\">a few </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">many</span> .</li> <span class=\"italic\">       \tExample: a few teaspoons </span>  <li>When a count noun is singular, we must use a word like a/the/my/this.</li>        \t<span class=\"italic\">Example: I am making a casserole.</span>  <li>When a countable noun is plural, we can use it alone.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: I love casseroles.</span> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Non-count nouns are things that we cannot divide into separate things.  They are materials, substances or amounts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>They are usually considered singular. You never put an s at the end.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: I added lobster and salmon to the pasta.</span>  <li>You can use <span class=\"strong\">some </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">any </span>  with non-count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: some butter </span>  <li>We can use <span class=\"strong\">a little </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">much </span>  with non-count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: a little garlic</span> </ul>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to prepare "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I prepared seafood pasta last night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about preparing meals, such as for family traditions."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entire "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "whole; complete "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I made enough food for the entire neighborhood!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "instead   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in the place of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I prepared a seafood casserole instead."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seafood  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a variety of species that live in the ocean, like lobster "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love seafood macaroni and cheese."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lobster "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large, red type of seafood "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Lobster is my favorite type of seafood."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feast "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very large meal "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your meal was a real feast!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "casserole "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a meal with meat and vegetables cooked together "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I made a seafood casserole last night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "butter "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a product made from milk, often used in cooking "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love cooking with butter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "celery  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long, thin light green vegetable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, I added celery to the casserole."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le04ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talk to friends or classmates from different countries, or search for information on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find information about 4 different cooking traditions in 4 different countries. What is the special occasion? What do people eat? How do they prepare food?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences about the traditions. You can start with <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIn Thailand ...\u201d</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Practice reading the sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information with a partner or the class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask and research about cooking traditions in different countries."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements about cooking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share the information with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le04ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  So, how did your original recipe for satay chicken sticks go last night?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span>: It was great! My girlfriend wants to visit Thailand to try the real thing. How was the seafood macaroni and cheese?", "id": 1, "time": "50", "image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Actually, I changed recipes. I prepared a seafood casserole instead. I bought the salmon from a local fisherman to make sure it was very fresh. I cooked it with butter and garlic. Then I started adding many things, like lobster, celery and broccoli.", "id": 2, "time": "14000", "image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span> : So your meal was a real feast!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, you could say that! I made enough food for the entire neighborhood!", "id": 3, "time": "36000", "image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span>: In my family, we often make casseroles to celebrate special occasions. Each member of the family has their favorite casserole.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  That's a nice family tradition.", "id": 4, "time": "45500", "image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Vocabulary and Grammar"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about food and customs."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express a goal or a purpose."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express general quantities."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What special traditions does your family have?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What foods do you prepare?